Xiv 2 days ago--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbstract twisted Brin--Thompson groups | ArxivLens (https://arxivlens.com/paperview/details/abstract-twisted-brin-thompson-groups-3037-cb470a79)\nciteturn3search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: last week; 2603.24687 Published Mar 25, 2026 ... In particular, if the Boone--Higman conjecture is true, then so is a related conjectural characterization of groups with solvable word problem, arising purely in the world of twisted Brin--Thompson groups.\n\nBack ArXiv math.GR Abstract twisted Brin--Thompson groups\n\nArXiv math.GR\n\n# Abstract twisted Brin--Thompson groups\n\nFrancesco Fournier-Facio, Matthew C. B. Zaremsky, Xiaolei Wu\n\n2603.24687 Published Mar 25, 2026\n\n### Publication\n\nPublished: Mar 25, 2026\n\nCategories: math.GR\n\n### Metrics\n\nSource: ArXiv\n\n### Paper Preview\n\n### Abstract\n\nGiven a group $G$ acting faithfully on a set $S$, one gets a simple group denoted $SV_G$, called a twisted Brin--Thompson group. In this paper we drop the faithfulness assumption, and get an abstract version of a twisted Brin--Thompson group $SV_G$. While the resulting group is not simple, since $SV_G$ surjects onto $SV_{G/\\ker(G \\curvearrowright S)}$, we prove that every proper normal subgroup of $SV_G$ lies in the kernel of this surjection, so $SV_G$ is ``relatively simple''. The advantage is that now we can prove that every finitely presented simple group embeds in a finitely presented abstract twisted Brin--Thompson group intersecting this kernel trivially. In particular, if the Boone--Higman conjecture is true, then so is a related conjectural characterization of groups with solvable word problem, arising purely in the world of twisted Brin--Thompson groups. We also prove a variety of additional results about abstract twisted Brin--Thompson groups, some of which are new even in the faithful case: they are all uniformly perfect, have property NL and property FW$_\\infty$, are boundedly acyclic and $\\ell^2$-invisible, and are $C^*$-simple as soon as they have trivial amenable radical. Along the way we formulate a new general criterion for $\\ell^2$-invisibility that is interesting in its own right.\n\n### OpenAlex\n\nCitations in OpenAlex\n    0\n\nPublication year\n    2026\n\nAccess status\n    Open access\n\nView on OpenAlex (opens in a new tab) Read open-access version (opens in a new tab)\n\nSource: OpenAlex · Snapshot 23 Sep 2026\n\n### Paper Details\n\nPaper ID: 2603.24687\n\nComments: 45 pages\n\nCategories:\n\nmath.GR\n\nView on arXiv Download PDF\n\n### Authors\n\nFF Francesco Fournier-Facio 24 papers MC Matthew C. B. Zaremsky 59 papers XW Xiaolei Wu 3 papers--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGraph theoretic properties of Speyer's matroid polynomial $g_M(t)$ — Scifaro (https://scifaro.com/en/abs/graph-theoretic-properties-of-speyer-s-matroid-polynomial-g-m-t-2506.18788)\nciteturn3search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Home › Combinatorics › Graph theoretic properties of Speyer's matroid polynomial $g… ...     @article{arxiv.2506.18788,\n\nHome › Combinatorics › Graph theoretic properties of Speyer's matroid polynomial $g…\n\n# Graph theoretic properties of Speyer's matroid polynomial $g_M(t)$\n\nCombinatorics 2025-06-24 v1\n\nAuthors: Erik Panzer\n\nView on arXiv ↗ PDF ↗\n\n### Abstract\n\nWe prove relations between the number of $k$k-connected components of a graph, Crapo's invariant $\\beta(M)$β(M) of a matroid, and Speyer's polynomial $g_M(t)$g M​(t). These yield a simple interpretation of $g_M'(-1)$g M′​(−1) when $M$M is graphic or cographic. Furthermore, we improve Ferroni's algorithm to compute $g_M(t)$g M​(t) and provide an implementation and an extensive data set. These calculations reveal a large number of graph theoretic constraints on the second derivative $g_M''(-1)$g M′′​(−1), which we thus advertise as